<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00585">
	<title>Temporarily pausing Cruise Control</title>
	<conbody>
		<table outputclass="formatc_none" frame="none" rowsep="0" colsep="0" id="e03718">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="0">
				<colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="2.343*" colsep="0"/>
				<colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="2.343*" colsep="0"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="0">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03719">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="images/N_SP3i26_B10_009_1_E.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>Cruise Control will be paused when:</p>
		<ul id="e03720">
			<li>
				<p>Depressing the brake pedal.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Pressing the (<image href="images/WKIA_079.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>) switch.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Shifting the gear to N (Neutral).</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Decreasing vehicle speed to less than approximately 30 km/h (20 mph).</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>ESC (Electronic Stability Control) is operating.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>The set speed will turn off but the Cruise (<image href="images/WKIA_357.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>) indicator will stay on.</p>
		<note type="note" id="e03721">
			<p>If Cruise Control pauses during a situation that is not mentioned, have the vehicle inspected by a professional workshop. Kia recommends visiting an authorized Kia dealer or service partner.</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
	<related-links>
